//! ds-tlsproxy — transparent + explicit TLS/HTTP proxy (doc 09 §5; doc 12).
//!
//! Built on pingora-core 0.8.1 (D40, vendored at TLS-1 prestage).
//!
//! # TLS-1 transparent listener
//!
//! Two TCP listeners receive traffic redirected by the nftables REDIRECT rules
//! (nft-1-bootstrap.nft, doc 03 §3 / doc 09 NFT-2):
//!
//!   - `:18080` for plaintext HTTP  (`iifname "dstap-*" tcp dport  80 redirect to :18080`)
//!   - `:18443` for HTTPS           (`iifname "dstap-*" tcp dport 443 redirect to :18443`)
//!
//! Both bind addresses are overridable via `DS_TLSPROXY_HTTP_ADDR` /
//! `DS_TLSPROXY_HTTPS_ADDR` (each a `host:port` SocketAddr; parse failure is
//! fatal). Unset ⇒ the `0.0.0.0:18080` / `0.0.0.0:18443` defaults above. The
//! override lets a bare-metal deploy rehome the HTTP leg off `:18080` when a
//! co-resident dev proxy already holds loopback:18080 (`0.0.0.0` covers it),
//! keeping the floor's `redirect to :<port>` target and the bind single-sourced.
//!
//! For each accepted connection:
//!
//!   1. Recover `original_dst` via `SocketDigest::original_dst()` (Pingora's
//!      SO_ORIGINAL_DST wrapper — D69 invariant 1: kernel source only, never
//!      inferred from anything the client sent).
//!   2. Refuse immediately if recovery fails (D69 invariant 3: refuse before
//!      reading a single client byte).
//!   3. Open a TCP upstream to `original_dst` (opaque tunnel at this prestage;
//!      TLS-3 re-origination lands when per-session-CA is wired, D17).
//!   4. Bidirectionally splice until both directions reach EOF.
//!
//! # Deferred integration seams (doc 12 §13.1)
//!
//! The following are explicit stubs documented here and in the guardrail map;
//! each is guarded by a `// TODO(seam:…)` comment below.
//!
//! - **Session attribution**: on the transparent path the per-tap `SessionRef`
//!   is now recovered at accept time from the **post-NAT local address** by one
//!   subtraction (`transparent::session_from_local_addr`, OQ1/D66 — doc 12
//!   §2.1 invariant 2 / §13.1, PROPOSED 2026-06-13): the accepted socket's
//!   `getsockname()` is the per-session host-side gateway `10.77.<idx>.0`, so
//!   `host_session_index` is its third octet and the `dstap-<idx>` tap name is
//!   the join key. Still deferred: the `session_uuid`/`host_id` join from the
//!   orchestrator session record (doc 14 §4 — left empty here) and the explicit
//!   path's attribution.
//!
//! - **SO_MARK** (D76): every upstream socket must carry
//!   `mark::compose(Leg::TlsproxyUpstream, session.host_session_index)` before
//!   any byte is sent. On the transparent path this is now **live** — driven by
//!   the `SessionRef` derived above; a local address that does not resolve to a
//!   session degrades to an unmarked best-effort connect (mark-only-adds, never
//!   gates).
//!
//! - **Admission check** (TLS-1 / D68): the SNI-checked admission decision —
//!   [`ds_tlsproxy::tls1_admission::decide`] — gates every HTTPS upstream connect
//!   BEFORE the opaque tunnel opens (peek the ClientHello SNI, refuse the
//!   ECH/absent-SNI/IP-literal edges, FORWARD-lookup `(session, sni_domain)` in
//!   the DNS-2b map and check `original_dst ∈ admitted_ips`, re-admit-not-refuse
//!   per D68). The DECISION is fully built and called below behind two inputs that
//!   are still seams: the per-tap [`SessionRef`] (seam:session-attribution) and the
//!   live admission-map read handle + policy snapshot (seam:admission). Until both
//!   land at M0-host integration, the HTTPS listener cannot construct the
//!   `(session, map, policy)` triple [`decide`] needs, so it tunnels opaquely as
//!   before — see [`tls1_gate`] for the honest call shape and what each seam
//!   supplies. The cross-service DNS-2 re-resolve a `ReAdmit` triggers is itself a
//!   further seam ([`ds_tlsproxy::tls1_admission::ReResolve`]).
//!
//! - **Telemetry** (D72 / D73): `ds-telemetry` event emission requires
//!   `SessionRef` and the policy-snapshot subscription channel.
//!
//! - **SeveringRegistry drive** (D53 / D76): the orchestrator revocation loop
//!   calls `RevocationSweep::apply()` on every policy-snapshot delta.  The
//!   registry is constructed here and will be passed to the orchestrator gRPC
//!   seam once it lands.
//!
//! - **HoldRegistry drive** (D46): pause/resume markers arrive over gRPC from
//!   the orchestrator; the registry is constructed here.
//!
//! Frozen non-edge (doc 12 §4.2, D76): ds-tlsproxy NEVER depends on ds-nft.
//! CAP_NET_RAW only — never CAP_NET_ADMIN.  A compromised proxy must not be
//! able to rewrite the ruleset that contains it.

